                  <msItem>
                     <title>Barlaam et Josaphat, etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Label pasted to fol. 2 with note of contents,
                        partly illegible, and pressmark (?) C.45 (?), and the later number
                        26.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">According to Young's catalogue, Geoffrey of
                        Monmouth followed the first item, but that is not noticed in the 1697
                        catalogue, in which this manuscript is Q. 57.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Though at Worcester in Herle's time and in
                        1623, when Young wrote his catalogue, this is probably not a medieval
                        Worcester book in view of the inscription, partly legible under UV, s. xv
                        ex: 'Iste liber constat . . . . . Py . . . magistro scolarum Sancti . . . .
                        ni (?) londoniarum'.</note>
                     <msItem>
                        <title>Barlaam et Josaphat (fol. 6-11).</title>
                     </msItem>
                     <msItem>
                        <title>De terrae partibus et provinciis eius (= Bartholomaeus Anglicus, lib.
                           XV; fol. 12-58).</title>
                     </msItem>
                     <msItem>
                        <author>Bede</author>
                        <title>De figuris verborum </title>
                     </msItem>
                  </msItem>
